# IsAIorNot API guidelines

Go Fiber API. Module path: `go-api`. Code and comments in **English**.

## Layers (dependency rule)

```
cmd/*/di → handler/{http,worker} → usecase → domain
                ↑                      ↑
         presenter (HTTP only)   repository/gorm + infrastructure (adapters)
```

- **domain** never imports `infrastructure`, `handler`, `usecase`, or `cmd`
- **usecase** depends only on `domain` (`entity`, `repository`, `port`, `paginate`, `media`, `messaging`, `realtime`, `aggregate`) — never concrete adapters
- Wire concrete implementations only in `cmd/*/di` (or `cmd/shared/pipeline`)

## Ports & adapters

- External deps (storage, Stripe, Centrifugo, RabbitMQ, analyzers, Clerk, video) go through `domain/port`
- Adapters live in `infrastructure/*` and implement those ports
- Vendor packages (`clerk`, `stripe`, `sightengine`, `rabbitmq`) stay under `infrastructure/` — OK to name by vendor there
- Prefer interface **values** in constructors: `repository.UserRepository`, not `*repository.UserRepository`

## Delivery split

- HTTP / webhooks / middleware / dto → `handler/http/`
- AMQP workers → `handler/worker/`
- Webhook Go types use business names (`UserWebhookHandler`, `BillingWebhookHandler`, `MediaUploadWebhookHandler`); HTTP routes may keep vendor paths (`/webhooks/clerk`, …)

## Naming

- Usecase packages by domain: `scan`, `media`, `subscription`, `identity` (not vendor names)
- Import aliases: `aimodelUseCase`, `pipelineUseCase` — not `aimodeluc`
- DI folders: `cmd/*/di` (manual composition, not google/wire)
- JSON tags for API/entities/presenters: **camelCase** (`scansCount`, `createdAt`)
- Do not camelCase external contracts (Clerk webhooks, MinIO `Records`, RabbitMQ payloads, Sightengine)

## Where new code goes

| Kind | Place |
|------|--------|
| Business flow | `usecase/<domain>/` |
| Entity / repo interface / port | `domain/` |
| GORM impl | `repository/gorm/` |
| External client | `infrastructure/<adapter>/` |
| HTTP response shape | `presenter/` |
| HTTP ingress DTO | `handler/http/dto/` |
| Composition root | `cmd/<binary>/di/` |

## Do not

- Put DTOs or helpers under `infrastructure/` unless they are adapter-specific
- Import adapters from usecases
- Rename pipeline stage `aimodel` / signal `ai_model` to a vendor name
- Expand scope beyond the request (no drive-by refactors)
